/*!
    \page creator-run-settings-harmonyos.html
    \previouspage creator-how-tos.html

    \ingroup creator-how-to-harmonyos

    \title Specify HarmonyOS run settings

    \brief Settings for running applications on HarmonyOS devices.

    To specify settings for running applications on the
    \l {Managing kits}{Run device} that you select for a kit, go to
    \uicontrol Projects > \uicontrol {Run Settings}.

    The application runs on the device inside the package that was deployed to
    it, so there is no executable to point at and no working directory to
    choose. What the run configuration does carry is the arguments the
    application is started with, which \QC passes to \c {aa start} and the
    application receives as its own \c argv.

    \uicontrol {Manage device configurations} opens
    \preferences > \uicontrol Devices > \uicontrol Devices, where the device
    the kit runs on is listed.

    \sa {HarmonyOS}{How to: Develop for HarmonyOS},
    {Developing for HarmonyOS devices},
    {Manage kits}{How to: Manage kits},
    {Configure projects for running}, {Managing kits},
    {Specify HarmonyOS deploy settings}
*/
